          "question": "my dads left arm has gone all achy n hes gone grey and sweaty, hes 62, is that somethin to worry about",
          "answer": "**Call emergency services now. Do not wait for further assessment.** A new ache in the left arm, grey skin and sweating in a 62-year-old man can be a sign of a heart attack. Call your local emergency number (999 in the UK, 911 in the US, 112 in the EU). Do not drive him yourself, and do not wait to see if it passes.\n\nThe risk tool returned \"routine\" because its fixed list did not match this description. I am not following that result. The chest pain guidance (red-flag-chest-pain) says that arm discomfort with a cold sweat should be treated as a possible heart attack until proven otherwise. It also lists breathlessness, nausea and light-headedness as warning signs, so tell the call handler about any of those too.\n\nWhile you wait:\n- Keep him sitting or lying down and keep him calm.\n- Loosen tight clothing.\n- Note when the symptoms started. Tell the call handler this.\n- Do not give him any medicine unless the emergency team tells you to. Ask them what to do.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
